    "turn_text": "That's right. And I am, I'm just so glad that to hear you thank you first of all the story. It's about that, the scene that you painted about that moment where your husband was having to drive himself and then him saying that he's not going to take part again. And yet, you know, after he passed, You being someone, again, I don't know if listeners heard this because you said it so quickly, but you are legally blind. And so you're transit dependent. And for you, and many, it is not an option to not take public transit. And you chose to fight for people to have the best possible transit and safety experience as possible in our in our community. And so I just really want to make that really clear listeners and reiterate and just you helping to connect the dots with telling me that story just really helped me even though you've told me that I've heard that story from you before just really brought it home again like why that was so meaningful for you and that was your entryway into becoming a public servant. And again, so District 12 is a district that you're running for, and it's a district that I live in, by the way, and I'm real proud resident of it and just thrilled. It is the second bluest house district in the country, according to the Cook Political Report, and I wanted to let people know again that some of your key endorsements have come from, you know, pretty significant endorsers' governor. Newsome, obviously, you mentioned, you know, Rep. Lee and state attorney. You've also been endorsed by Emily's list. These, you know, some big organizations that endorse, you know, and have very significant winning records of those who they've backed. Emily's list higher heights for America, which backs African American women candidates and labor groups such as California Working Families Party and S-E-I-U. As Steve mentioned and you mentioned, you gained 56% of the vote in the primary earlier this month that you had said was odd, but when you were saying about your history of how much work you put in and you are one of the hardest working people, I don't even know how you do it. But yes, you got that 56% of the vote. By the way, Democratic Jennifer Tran came in second, second with the most votes at 15%. So my question is, how are you and your team then gearing up for the general election?",
