  {
    "episode_id": 45245,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45245.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "You can't really take anything for granted, ever. Our lives are really on the line in this election. I have over the last five days, I've done 16 events, and I've been working on my day job in the morning and at night. I believe that we will win, but so much of how I'm looking at this election is, both locally and nationally, is about both my on the groundwork here to convince us to turn out for my race, but also for the Democratic Party and for local races here. You know, I just met with the Delta's and they had a big, huge convening. It was like a thousand people in the room. And these are black women who are committed to social action. It's a C3. But for me, what is so important is that everywhere I am, especially locally, like it, I want to be out every single day on the ground, at, you know, at doors, at community meetings. I am tabling tomorrow at the flea market. I hope it doesn't rain. to talk about the development opportunities in South Berkeley for black people who have been, you know, pushed out for the last 50 years. I have like so many messages, but one of the messages that I have for folks who are involved in politics is that we have a, like, we have a sinister beast that is coming from, again, the Trump administration, the Trump administration, from the Trump campaign, but also in the re-vert a progressivism in the Bay Area. We are going to become Orange County very, very soon. This idea that we can revert back to even my good friends who are in government to a 1980s failed policy strategy about how we deal with poverty and addiction and crime. I was at the Niagara Movement dinner the other night. And there were some of those folks in the audience. And it's like, we don't have to tear each other apart. We just actually have to be very honest with each other. You're wrong. We go love each other, but sure wrong. So for me, it is continuing to be steadfast, even in this moment of the modernization of progressivism in the Bay Area, knowing that we have big fights to fight NTC. We know what those are. And also, we have a politic to keep center. here in the Bay Area. We know, we know real strategies to solve these old problems. We just got to curtail our folks to get in line to do the right thing. So I am going to have an amazing ground game. I still have endorsements to get. And I have another 500,000 people to talk to. So yes, I'm going to win. I need to support, again, the Biden-Harris campaign. There are campaigns in red and purple states that I promised leader Jeffries that I was going to be on the ground. I met with him. He gave me an hour at his time a couple of weeks ago and asked my adult daughter to enjoy the meeting. The staff called me and said, here you have a daughter in DC. I'm making relationships in DC so that my transition with Ms. Lee's office is amazing. I'm working hard because our people deserve it, right? Our people deserve it. We need to be in the house.",
